{
  "_comment": "Loot tables for the item-drops + crafting lane. Loaded by DeNelle.Village.Items.LootTableCatalog via DeNelle.Core.CanonicalJson (Resources first, StreamingAssets fallback). Gated by ItemDropSystem.Enabled (ON for V1). ItemDropWatcher keys a table by the slain enemy's EnemyDefId (enemies.json id); if none matches it falls back to defaults.enemy / defaults.boss. WO Consumable-Crafting-V1 added per-enemy tables for the real V1 roster (orc + hollow families) dropping the 12 art-backed ingredients (materials.json). The legacy common-grunt / boss-hoard tables remain as the fallback defaults.",
  "_schemaNotes": {
    "tables": "Each table maps an enemy/boss def id (enemies.json) to weighted drops. 'source' is documentation only (enemy/boss/dungeon).",
    "drops": "Each line is rolled INDEPENDENTLY: roll 'chance' (0..1); on a hit award a random count in [minCount, maxCount]. materialId is deposited into VillageInventory (the village larder) - it is a materials.json ingredient id.",
    "bossOnly": "WO-556: optional bool per drop line (default false). A bossOnly line ONLY rolls on a BOSS kill (table source 'boss', or DragonBoss). Used to gate the GEM crystals (ing_ember_crystal/ing_aether_shard/ing_heartstone_crystal) behind bosses at a low rate; ordinary mobs skip them.",
    "defaults": "Fallback table ids used when a slain enemy/boss has no table of its own."
  },
